{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>One bull, a son of cattle.</b> Of the congregation, and likewise one ram, and they are not the bull of the high priest or his ram. In my opinion, the ram mentioned in the section of Aḥarei Mot that was taken from the people is not this one, for concerning his ram and the ram of the people it is said “and he shall make his burnt offering and the burnt offering of the people.” And the proof is that there is an addition of seven lambs; also this “one male goat for a sin offering” is not the goat of the lots. Therefore it is written: “besides the sin offering of the atonements, which is written in the section of Aḥarei Mot.”"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "Resolved האיל שלו as 'his ram,' i.e., the high priest's ram, consistent with the context of Leviticus 16."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:48.976842857Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}